// Real geometry (unlike farm01/warehouse01/02, which still point at
// house01.nbt as a placeholder) — the lumberjack's hut, main building only.
// The tree farm this belongs to isn't designed yet:
//   - whether the footprint stays FromBlueprint or widens to reserve ground
//     for Anno-style farm tiles placed around it (working radius, tile
//     count -> production %) is still open;
//   - `production` is left out entirely rather than stubbed, since output
//     here is meant to land in an in-world chest rather than an abstract
//     buffer (078's model), and nothing scans a blueprint for chest
//     positions yet. The exported .nbt now has chests in it for exactly
//     that; the catalogue/definition loaders don't read block entities at
//     all yet (roadmap: block entities are dropped on write).
// Both come back once the tree-farm mechanic itself is settled.
Building(
    name: "Lumberjack's Hut",
    blueprint: "lumber.nbt",
    tier: 1,
    requires: [],
    category: Production,
    footprint: FromBlueprint,
    cost: [
        (block: "minecraft:oak_planks", count: 20),
        (block: "minecraft:oak_log", count: 10),
    ],
    integrity: Integrity(
        pristine_above: 0.95,
        ruined_below: 0.60,
    ),
)
